  nonce: 598d  # 598d
  message: "CURE (1) IS RE-SCOPED BY THE OWNER'S A+no RULING (2026-09-21), shipped as ADR-0058 in PR #1115 (0d53994326).\n\nWHAT CHANGED FOR THIS ROW. `Symbol.signature` no longer declares `free-text -- never branch on the value`; it declares the callable-signature axis. The nine consumers that parse the value are GRANDFATHERED AND CLOSED: `signature_axis.find_undeclared_value_parsers` fails the suite on a tenth. Cure (2) (`method_call_recovery._declares_non_callable_value`) is the ninth and keeps working.\n\nSO THE OBVIOUS ROUTE IS SHUT, DELIBERATELY. All four residual shapes read a DECLARED TYPE and `Symbol.signature` was the only place Python recorded one -- verified per shape, not carried:\n  factory return    `_file_synth_run = AnalysisRun.create(...)`   -> needs `create`'s return annotation\n  property chain    `ts.workspace.add`  (`def workspace(self) -> Store`) -> needs the getter's return annotation\n  builtin receiver  `handler_map.get(...)` (`handler_map: dict[str, Any]` at hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py:3777) -> needs a variable annotation\n  loop targets      element type of the iterable\nReading any of them out of the signature string would be the tenth parse. The gate refuses it.\n\nTHE ROUTE THAT IS OPEN, and it is not a new build. Four declared homes already ship and Python writes exactly one:\n  FileAnalysis.method_return_types (base.py:227) <- go, rust, swift, objc   python: NO\n  meta[\"return_type\"]                            <- java, luau, apex        python: NO\n  meta[\"parameters\"] / [\"params\"]                <- 15 analyzers            python: YES\n  FileAnalysis.class_field_types  (base.py:189)  <- csharp, cpp             python: NO\npy.py:641 cites the first one in a comment 5,240 lines above py.py:5881, where it parses the string instead.\n\nFILED: WI-ribak -- py.py populates the two registries in Pass 1 and re-points py.py:5881 at the aggregated `_method_return_type_registry`. Linked isbefore: WI-ribak blocks this row, because every residual site needs a declared-type source and there is no longer a legal second one.\n\nA PATH-REFERENCE AMBIGUITY IN THE ENUMERATION, fixed here: the row's `cli.py:3777` is the TRACKER package's cli.py (`packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py`), not hypergumbo-core's. Probing core's first landed in an unrelated pip-install block. Same for `stop_hook.py:280` -> `packages/hypergumbo-tracker/src/hypergumbo_tracker/stop_hook.py`.\n\nSTATUS AND PRIORITY UNCHANGED: todo_soft, P2. 14 of the original 16 still live.\n\nNOT RE-MEASURED HERE: the 14 are still carried from #1113's diff. ADR-0058 changed no analyzer output -- it is a declaration plus a consumer gate -- so no drift is expected, but that is an argument, not a survey. The next agent to work this row should re-run the repro before building on the count, which is the mistake this row has now collected twice."  # 598d
