  set:  # 7532
    description: "The residue WI-rulik's gate does not reach.\n\nCURRENT STATE IS POST-#1113 (cure (2) shipped 2026-09-21): **62 edges, 14 wrong** -- artifact `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fihun_after/survey.json`. The two `[field]` sites at the foot of the list below are CURED and struck; the other 14 are unchanged in site and mechanism.\n\nAS FILED AND RE-VERIFIED PRE-CURE against `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/togad_after/survey.json` -- the post-ADR-0057 §14.1 state: **64 edges, 16 wrong.** Four statements in the original filing were wrong or have drifted; each is corrected in place below and listed at the end.\n\nTHE MECHANISM. The stub ABSTAINED on its module (`dst_ref is None`), so WI-rulik's refusal does not fire; the class-hint set has more than one member with a method of that short name; and the line-proximity tiebreaker -- `method_call_recovery.py:302`, `key=lambda pair: (abs(pair[0].line - ucall.line), pair[0].id)` -- picks the wrong one. `_declared_receiver_type` reads `receiver_type_hint`, and the filter drops a hint that CONTRADICTS a stamped type but abstains when nothing is stamped: correct polarity, almost never armed. The hint is RARE rather than absent -- 806 of 62,384 Python unresolved-call edges carry one (1.3%) -- and 0 of the 90 stubs behind these edges did.\n\nTHE 16 AS FILED -- 14 STILL LIVE, 2 CURED (file:line -> what it bound, vs what the receiver actually is):\n  all_analyzers.py:533   `_file_synth_run.to_dict()` is an AnalysisRun -> Limits.to_dict\n  compact.py:1606        `sym.to_dict()` is a Symbol          -> CompactResult.to_dict\n  test_compact.py:3828   `s.to_dict()` over all_symbols       -> Span.to_dict\n  test_compact.py:3898   same                                  -> Span.to_dict\n  test_ir.py:1432        `ctx.to_dict()` is a UsageContext     -> Span.to_dict\n  test_ir.py:2863        `e.to_dict()` is an Edge              -> ExternalRef.to_dict\n  test_schema.py:578     `instance.to_dict()` over {Symbol, Edge, AnalysisRun} -> ExternalRef.to_dict\n  test_sketch.py:7058    -> Edge.to_dict\n  hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py:3777   `handler_map.get(...)` is a dict (declared `dict[str, Any]`) -> TrackerSet.get\n  hypergumbo_tracker/stop_hook.py:280   `set.add`                        -> TrackerSet.add\n  test_fork_workflow.py  `ts.workspace.add` (TrackerSet.workspace returns a Store) -> TrackerSet.add  [4 sites: 108, 168, 191, 218]\n  id_matching.py:119     `m.start()` / `m.end()` on a re.Match -> ItemIdMatch.start / .end  [2 sites, kind=field]  ** CURED by #1113 -- no longer emitted **\n\nWHAT IS AT STAKE (established after this row was filed). ADR-0057 §14.1 (WI-togad) made a resolved edge able to demote the stub it NAMES, and this linker now stamps `derived_from` on all 64 of its edges -- the provenance is recorded and true. But `docs/audits/0020-recovery-linker-supersession-precision.md` REFUSES this pass the `supersedes_consumed_stub` permission on exactly this measurement (16 of 64 = 25% wrong), where `inherited-calls-linker` was granted it (0 of 70 wrong). The refusal was not conditioned on a quality signal because none separates the wrong edges: `disambiguation_fallback` is set on 5 of the 16 wrong and 13 of the 48 right, a 28% versus 24% wrong rate -- refusing at random. **So the 45 supersessions this pass would have carried stay unrecorded until it has receiver evidence to be right with.** That is what fixing this row buys, and it is why the fix is the producer-side one.\n\nTWO CURES, and they are not alternatives -- the first is the real one and is ALL THAT REMAINS. Cure (2) SHIPPED in #1113 and took the 2 field sites; the 14 live sites are all cure (1)'s.\n\n(1) MAKE THE EVIDENCE EXIST. The Python analyzer does not stamp `receiver_type_hint` for these shapes (local variable assigned from a constructor, a parameter with an annotation, a comprehension target, an attribute chain). Every one of the 16 has a receiver whose type the repository states somewhere. This is the same drain WI-zilag / WI-dizag / WI-doluf ran for other languages' module slots, applied to the hint this linker already knows how to consume. Refusing to guess is cheap; supplying the evidence is what actually recovers the edge. Sizing note: the hint's 1.3% population is the coverage gap to close, not a from-zero build -- the stamping path exists and works.\n\n(2) A CALLABILITY GATE, for the 2 field cases. **SHIPPED #1113** as `method_call_recovery._declares_non_callable_value`; kept below for the reasoning, which still governs any widening. `ItemIdMatch.start` is declared `int`; binding a `calls` edge to it is outside this linker's own premise (it stamps `call_construct=\"method\"`). A blanket `kind == \"field\"` refusal is NOT safe -- a JS/TS class property and a Python dataclass field can both hold a callable, and `js_ts.py` records `property_signature` members as `field`. The safe polarity is a POSITIVE refusal: refuse when the member's DECLARED TYPE is present and names a non-callable (`Symbol.signature` carries `str` / `int` / `Optional[str]` for all 28 field targets measured), never when it is absent.\n\nWHERE CURE (2) LANDED -- and a correction. It shipped WITHOUT the declared taxonomy discussed here, by discriminating on a parenthesis (`int` is a value type, `(self) -> int` is a signature), which sidesteps the callable-KINDS question entirely. The taxonomy below remains the right home if the gate is ever widened. The original filing reported `ranking.py` `_CALLABLE_KINDS = {\"function\", \"method\"}` and `entrypoints.py` `frozenset({\"function\", \"method\", \"constructor\"})` as two hardcoded sets that \"disagree\", and proposed folding them. **They disagree BY DESIGN, and have said so since 28d26c92c8 (2026-05-05), four months before this row was filed.** Each site names the other and states the reason: ranking's is deliberately narrower because \"constructors carry the class name, so name-conflict dampening on them would penalise normal Java/C# style\", and entrypoints' includes constructors because \"a service object's `__init__` wires up dependencies and forms a real graph hub\". Both are marked forward-compatible. So there is no inconsistency to fold, and a fold would be a regression in two separate rankers. What survives: a `callability` taxonomy over the language_construct axis -- `SymbolKindSpec.type_family` is the shipped precedent (audit-findings 0018) for adding a queryable subset without ADR-0024's machinery -- could give cure (2) a DECLARED home instead of a third hardcoded set, with each existing site declaring which subset it wants rather than being merged into one. Assignment must be evidence-driven and under-assignment must be the SAFE direction, which it is only if the gate refuses on declared non-callability rather than requiring declared callability.\n\nNOT ASSERTED: that the other 48 edges are correct -- they were not individually audited, only the 16 known-wrong were. Nor that cure (1) is cheap; it is a producer-side drain across several receiver shapes. Nor that any of this generalises off this repository: one Python-heavy corpus, as `docs/audits/0020` also says of the grant it issued.\n\nREPRO: `hypergumbo survey . --out survey.json`, select edges whose `origin` contains `method-call-recovery-linker` (`origin` is a LIST), read each against its source line; the symbol's file is `path`, not `file`. Artifact: `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/togad_after/survey.json` (current state). `rulik_after/survey.json` is the original filing's artifact and PREDATES §14.1 -- use it only for before/after on the demotion counts.\n\nCORRECTED FROM THE ORIGINAL FILING, by re-measurement rather than re-reading:\n  - the count was \"17 of 64\" in the title and \"45 known-wrong\" in NOT ASSERTED; the enumerated list, `docs/audits/0020` (`wrong_in_audit: 16`) and the survey all say **16**. Title fixed.\n  - the tiebreaker line reference `method_call_recovery.py:270` was stale after WI-togad edited the file; it is **:302**.\n  - \"no receiver evidence is consulted because none exists\" overstated it: the hint exists on 1.3% of Python unresolved calls, and on none of the 90 stubs audited here.\n  - the two `_CALLABLE_KINDS` sets do not disagree by accident, and must not be folded (above)."  # 7532
- op: discuss  # 909a
  at: '2026-09-21T07:26:47Z'  # 909a
  by: agent  # 909a
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 909a
  clock: 10  # 909a
  nonce: 909a  # 909a
  message: "BLOCKER CLEARED. WI-ribak is done (PR #1117, c9652b836e): python stamps `Symbol.meta[\"return_type\"]` in Pass 1 and reads it, so a callee's declared return type now has a home this repository actually populates -- 4 -> 31,932 symbols carry it.\n\nWHAT THAT UNBLOCKS HERE, and what it does NOT.\n\nAVAILABLE NOW: the return-type shapes. A factory (`_file_synth_run = AnalysisRun.create(...)`) and a property chain (`ts.workspace.add`, where `def workspace(self) -> Store`) both need a callee's declared return type, and it is now readable from meta by ANY consumer -- including a core linker, which py.py's own FileAnalysis could never have reached. That is roughly 7 of the 14.\n\nSTILL WITHOUT A HOME: the other shapes read a VARIABLE's or FIELD's declared type, not a callable's return type -- `handler_map: dict[str, Any]` at hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py:3777, the loop/comprehension element types. `FileAnalysis.class_field_types` exists in the tree-sitter base (csharp, cpp) but python writes it and it is not a Symbol-carried fact, so it does not reach a linker either. There is NO registered meta key for a field's declared type. Declaring one is ADR-0024 creation practice and a separate argument, not something to fold into a linker PR.\n\nSO THE NEXT MOVE ON THIS ROW IS THE RETURN-TYPE SUBSET, and the residual splits: ~7 reachable, ~7 waiting on a field-type home.\n\nNOT RE-MEASURED: the 14 are still carried from #1113's diff. WI-ribak's survey diff showed this linker's 62 edges IDENTICAL before and after, so nothing disturbed them -- but that is evidence they were not disturbed, not a fresh audit of the 14. Re-run the repro before building on the count."  # 909a
- op: discuss  # 44f8
  at: '2026-09-21T07:50:11Z'  # 44f8
  by: agent  # 44f8
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 44f8
  clock: 11  # 44f8
  nonce: 44f8  # 44f8
  message: "INVESTIGATED THE RESIDUAL AND THE \"FOUR SHAPES\" ARE REALLY THREE BLOCKERS, each located. This replaces the row's shape-level description, which named symptoms rather than causes.\n\nBLOCKER 1 -- THE RETURN-TYPE INFERENCE ONLY FIRES FOR A BARE FUNCTION CALL.\npy.py's var_types seeding (now py.py:5898, reading meta[\"return_type\"] since WI-ribak) is reached only when `_resolve_call_target` returns a function/method Symbol. Probed directly, one file each:\n    c = make()          bare function            -> c.send() RESOLVES\n    c = f.build()       f: Factory, instance     -> f.build() is itself UNRESOLVED, so no type\n    c = Cls.create()    classmethod on the class -> Cls.create() is itself UNRESOLVED, so no type\nSo the FACTORY sites (all_analyzers.py:533, `_file_synth_run = AnalysisRun.create(...)`) fail BEFORE the declared return type is ever consulted. The evidence is present and unused: that call edge already carries receiver_type_hint=\"AnalysisRun\" plus a receiver_type_id. What is missing is resolving `Cls.method()` / `obj.method()` to the callee Symbol, not the return type -- WI-ribak did not and could not help here.\n\nBLOCKER 2 -- `Name.attr.method()` HAS NO BRANCH AT ALL.\nThe attribute-receiver emit path is guarded by `isinstance(func, ast.Attribute) and isinstance(func.value, ast.Name)` (py.py:8093). For `ts.workspace.add(1)` the func.value is itself an ast.Attribute, so the chain never enters that block and no receiver hint is stamped. BOTH HALVES ALREADY EXIST and nothing joins them, verified on a probe file:\n    the `ts.workspace` edge carries receiver_type_hint=\"TrackerSet\" (ts = TrackerSet(...) is a constructor, so var_types types it)\n    `TrackerSet.workspace` carries meta[\"return_type\"] = \"Store\"   (a property with a plain annotation)\nJoining them -- receiver Name in var_types, attr is a member of that class, read the member's declared return type, resolve it to a project class, stamp the hint -- cures the 4 test_fork_workflow sites (108/168/191/218). That is the HIGHEST-VALUE next step on this row and the only residual shape whose evidence is fully present today.\n\nBLOCKER 3 -- THE BUILTIN-RECEIVER SITES HAVE NO EVIDENCE ANYWHERE.\n`handler_map: dict[str, Any]` (hypergumbo_tracker/cli.py:3777) is a function-LOCAL. It is not emitted as a Symbol at all -- confirmed by searching the survey's nodes for the name -- so its annotation is recorded nowhere and no consumer can read it. There is also no registered meta key for a variable's or field's declared type. This is not a linker problem and cannot be fixed from the linker; it needs a producer decision about symbolising annotated locals, which is its own argument.\n\nWHAT SHIPPED HERE, AND WHAT IT DID NOT DO. A quoted forward reference is now accepted as a type name (`-> \"Client\"`), since ast.unparse renders string annotations with their quotes and PEP 484 says such an annotation names exactly the type it spells. Tested, and mutation-checked both ways. **It fixes ZERO of the 14 sites, and the measured effect on this repository is ZERO**: 37 of 31,932 stamped return types are quoted, and none currently sits in a bare-function assignment, the only position blocker 1 leaves open. It is shipped as a latent-correctness fix and a prerequisite for the factory shape once blocker 1 is addressed -- not as a recall claim. Survey diff vs ribak_after: resolved calls 0 lost / 16 gained (all 16 from the new test file's own code), method-call-recovery edges 62 -> 62 IDENTICAL, receiver hints 810 -> 810.\n\nSO THE COUNT IS UNCHANGED: 14 of the original 16 remain. The split by blocker is 3 factory (blocker 1) - 4 property chain (blocker 2) - 5 loop/comprehension targets (needs container element typing, not investigated here) - 2 builtin receivers (blocker 3).\n\nSTILL NOT RE-MEASURED: the 14 themselves are carried from #1113's diff. Two surveys since have shown this linker's 62 edges IDENTICAL each time, which is evidence they were not disturbed -- not a fresh audit of which 14 are wrong."  # 44f8
- op: discuss  # 43bc
  at: '2026-09-21T08:06:56Z'  # 43bc
  by: agent  # 43bc
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 43bc
  clock: 12  # 43bc
  nonce: 43bc  # 43bc
  message: "SHIPPED: PR #1118, merged 0c611ba000 -- the quoted-forward-reference fix described in the diagnosis above. THE SITE COUNT IS UNCHANGED AT 14 OF 16 and this row stays todo_soft; the fix addresses none of them and its measured effect on this repository was zero.\n\nWHAT IS NOW TRUE OF THIS ROW'S RESIDUAL:\n  3 factory returns   -> blocked by blocker 1 (Cls.create() / obj.build() are themselves unresolved, so no declared return type is ever consulted)\n  4 property chain    -> WI-fikoh, filed and linked isbefore this row; all evidence present today\n  5 loop/comprehension targets -> needs container element typing; NOT investigated, no blocker located\n  2 builtin receivers -> blocker 3 (handler_map is a function-local, never emitted as a Symbol, so its dict[str, Any] annotation is recorded nowhere)\n\nThe honest state: WI-fikoh is the only residual shape that can be worked today. The factory shape needs Cls.method() / obj.method() call resolution first -- a separate producer change nobody has filed. The loop-target shape has not been looked at. The builtin shape needs a producer decision about symbolising annotated locals."  # 43bc
